{"Test docstring contradicts test assertion - docstring says errors in processing don't block offset commits for other messages but assertion checks that no commits happen at all": 0.5354210734367371, "close() loses offsets completed during worker drain - commit thread is stopped before queue pool workers are drained, causing offsets completed between commit_thread.join() and queue_pool.shutdown() to never be committed to Kafka, resulting in message reprocessing on consumer restart": 0.9606184959411621, "Error handling test is flaky due to timing - test only passes because commit loop's first iteration is delayed by shutdown_event.wait(1.0), and on slower systems the commit loop could fire before the assertion is checked": 0.612532377243042, "terminate() doesn't stop commit thread, leaking it - terminate() sets shutdown event and shuts down queue pool but never joins the commit thread, which may continue attempting commits against a shut-down queue pool and log spurious errors": 0.9091044068336487}